{
  "id": "practice-lab",
  "name": "Practice home lab",
  "summary": "The same home lab with three mistakes hidden in it. Open Checks to find them; each Why? says what went wrong and how to fix it.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "claim": "Every address in this sample is private address space (192.168.0.0/16), so nothing here names a real network.",
      "cite": "RFC 1918, Address Allocation for Private Internets, section 3, Private Address Space",
      "url": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1918.html",
      "read_on": "2026-10-10"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Device models, their port counts and which switch ports give PoE are the catalogue's, and cite their own sources there.",
      "cite": "corpus/catalogue/ (each model's own source block)",
      "url": "",
      "read_on": "2026-10-10"
    },
    {
      "claim": "A VLAN on its own does not keep two networks apart once a router joins them. UniFi's zone-based firewall shows Internal to Internal as Allow All by default, and its Network Isolation option is what adds the rules that block traffic between VLANs. So this sample's router carries a rule that stops the cameras reaching the LAN.",
      "cite": "Ubiquiti Help Center: Zone-Based Firewalls in UniFi (zone matrix, Internal to Internal: Allow All); Implementing Network and Client Isolation in UniFi (Network Isolation configures the firewall rules that block inter-VLAN traffic)",
      "url": "https://help.ui.com/hc/en-us/articles/115003173168",
      "read_on": "2026-10-25"
    }
  ],
